The most recent Audi A4 with a naturally aspirated FSI V6 engine is the B8 generation (2008-2011) with the 3.2 FSI V6 engine. This engine produced 265 HP and 243.4 lb-ft of torque. It was available with Quattro all-wheel drive and either a 6-speed manual, 6-speed Tiptronic automatic, or Multitronic CVT transmission. The 0-60 mph time is around 5.9-6.3 seconds depending on the transmission. Fuel economy is rated around 26-31 mpg UK combined (21-26 mpg US). The car's dimensions are approximately 4703 mm (185.16 in) long, 1826 mm (71.89 in) wide, and 1427-1436 mm (56.18-56.54 in) high, with a wheelbase of 2808 mm (110.55 in). Cargo space is around 480 liters (16.95 cu ft) for the sedan. Ground clearance is around 10.8-12.9 cm (4.25-5.08 inches). The turning circle is 11.5 m (37.73 ft).

Used prices for a B8 A4 3.2 FSI Quattro in the UK range from around £6,996 to £7,995 on Auto Trader. On AutoScout24, a 2011 model with 187,000 km is listed for €13,500 (approx $14,500 USD). Used prices are generally well below the average new car price today.

Common issues reported for the B8 A4 generation include oil consumption (especially in 2.0 TFSI, but V6 can also have issues), timing chain tensioner failure, carbon buildup on intake valves, ignition coil/spark plug issues, and high-pressure fuel pump problems. Recalls included issues with the coolant pump, airbags, fuel injector rails, auxiliary heater element, and brake servo vacuum line.

The interior was considered high-quality for its time with features like the MMI system, though the technology is dated by modern standards. ADAS features were minimal or optional. Smartphone connectivity like Apple CarPlay or Android Auto was not available. USB ports were not standard; connectivity was typically via proprietary Audi Music Interface or aux-in.

